156 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 87 0 R
/E (The most satisfying experience in my career has been to guide students in interdisciplinary research. I managed the students of the first batch of Chemical Engineering in the projects based on machine learning with Design of Experiments and the result was published in Bioresource Technology \(impact factor 11.4 at the time\). Other innovative concepts on which I have been working in the field of quantum cryptography are the application of chaotic systems to create randomness in a quantum key distribution. Recently, we have published our work on the aerodynamic design and optimization in Aerospace science and technology.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
157 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 87 0 R
/E (I would say to students that mathematics is a field that is fundamental to science and technological development. Linear algebra is the foundation of such areas as artificial intelligence and quantum computing, whereas abstract algebra and number theory are at the heart of post-quantum cryptography, which will protect cyberspace against future quantum attacks. The need to have such foundations is highlighted in initiatives made by bodies like NIST. I want my students to be curious, work hard, and appreciate mathematics because what may come out as an abstract concept in this day and age may turn out to be the breakthroughs in the near future.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
