<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 89 0 R
/E (LQG also addresses the singularity problem. Because spacetime cannot be compressed below the Planck scale, collapse does not produce infinite density. Instead, it reaches a minimum scale and undergoes a quantum bounce. Effective models suggest the black hole interior transitions into an expanding region resembling a white hole. In this way, a consistent quantum theory of gravity resolves classical singularities and offers a coherent description of extreme gravitational regimes.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
