244 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 93 0 R
/E (Muhammad Sohail Ahmad \(Batch 20-24\) explored the phenomenon of atomic coherence through his FYP titled "Study of Atomic Coherence in Electromagnetically Induced Grating," in which he compared the degree of polarization rotation of a probe beam in EIT and EIG configurations, research with direct applications in laser frequency stabilization, laser locking, and quantum sensing. He is now pursuing a Master's degree in Optics at Shanxi University, Taiyuan, China, where his research focuses on continuous variable quantum information processing, including a current project on Bessel beams as candidates for quantum dense coding. His scholarship from Shanxi University covers full tuition, accommodation, and a monthly stipend, and he studies within the Institute of Optoelectronics, which is ranked 2nd in China for quantum research. His message to juniors: Dream beyond borders, believe beyond limits, stay curious, work hard, and remember your future is bigger than you think.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [6]
>>
