1484 0 obj
<<
/Title (In 2025, scientists from collaborations like Fermilab and the University of Chicago found evidence that dark energy might change over time, challenging the standard cosmological model that assumes it is constant. By analyzing galaxy distributions, they detected deviations from predictions based on a constant cosmological constant. These provisional findings suggest that evolving physics could drive the universe's accelerated expansion, potentially requiring significant revisions in modern cosmology if confirmed.)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1475 0 R
>>
endobj
